    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286-a1-a5">

                <pb facs="0256" n="236" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg236"/>

                <head>E.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters 3d New Hampshire
                                Vols.,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Bermuda Hundred, Va.,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 28, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to state that Emile Caulet
                    was mustered into service as per endorsement from your office; that he was
                    wounded at Drury’s Bluff, May 16, 1864, and died May 22, 1864; and I have no
                    doubt that he is the man referred to by Mr. Geofroy as A. Cauvet.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">J. J. PLIMPTON, <hi rendition="#italic">Lieut. Col.,
                        Comd’g</hi> 3<hi rendition="#italic">d New Hampshire Vols.</hi></p>
                <p>Brigadier General L. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Adjutant General U. S. Army, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                <p>Official copy:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. D. TOWNSEND, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Adjutant
                        General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
